### What version of the Codex App are you using (From “About Codex” dialog)?

ChatGPT desktop 26.1013.40934 (build 20770), using the Codex/local-work in-app Browser. Version read from the installed ChatGPT.app bundle metadata.

### What subscription do you have?

Not provided. This rendering failure reproduces on a standalone local HTML page before any model request.

### What platform is your computer?

macOS 15.7.4 (24G517), Apple Silicon; uname -mprs: Darwin 24.6.0 arm64 arm

### What issue are you seeing?

The desktop in-app Browser loads an ordinary localhost page, but iframe documents navigated to locally created blob: URLs remain at about:blank. Equivalent HTTP and srcdoc iframe documents render correctly. Fetching the same blob URL successfully returns its contents.

The standalone reproduction below uses generated placeholder text and does not require authentication, application code, or remote resources.

Observed in the in-app Browser:

| Test | Result |
| --- | --- |
| Same-origin HTTP iframe | Content rendered |
| srcdoc iframe | Content rendered |
| HTML blob iframe | Document stayed about:blank |
| XHTML blob iframe | Document stayed about:blank |
| Blob URL assigned before iframe insertion | Document stayed about:blank |
| Visible blob iframe (not display:none) | Document stayed about:blank |
| Sandboxed blob iframe | Document stayed about:blank |
| Sandboxed XHTML blob iframe inside a closed shadow root | Document stayed about:blank |
| fetch(blobURL) | Correct content returned |

Refreshing the in-app Browser did not resolve the blank iframe content in this session.

Connected Chrome rendered blob-backed iframe content correctly during testing, with no logged browser warnings/errors.

The exact internal browser cause is not established; this report describes the observable blob-iframe navigation failure, not a confirmed CSP or WebKit diagnosis.

### What steps can reproduce the bug?

1. Serve a directory on loopback, for example with python3 -m http.server 5181 --bind 127.0.0.1.
2. Put the following in index.html and create frame.html containing <!doctype html><body>HTTP frame loaded</body>.
3. Open http://127.0.0.1:5181/ in the desktop in-app Browser.
4. Compare the HTTP/srcdoc documents with the blob documents, and compare the successful fetch results with iframe.contentDocument.URL.

Reduced form of the standalone probe used during diagnosis:

```html
<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Iframe loading probe</title>
<div id="tests"></div>
<script>
const html = '<!doctype html><html><body>HTML frame loaded</body></html>';
const xhtml = '<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><title>Chapter</title></head><body><p>XHTML frame loaded</p></body></html>';
for (const mode of ['http', 'srcdoc', 'blob-html', 'blob-xhtml']) {
  const section = document.createElement('section');
  const label = document.createElement('h2');
  label.textContent = mode;
  const status = document.createElement('pre');
  const fetched = document.createElement('pre');
  const frame = document.createElement('iframe');
  section.append(label, status, fetched, frame);
  document.querySelector('#tests').append(section);
  function report() {
    try {
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      status.textContent = 'document=' + doc?.URL +
        '\ntext=' + doc?.body?.textContent;
    } catch (error) {
      status.textContent = String(error);
    }
  }
  frame.addEventListener('load', report);
  frame.addEventListener('error', () => {
    status.textContent = 'iframe error';
  });
  if (mode === 'http') frame.src = './frame.html';
  else if (mode === 'srcdoc') frame.srcdoc = html;
  else {
    const xml = mode === 'blob-xhtml';
    frame.src = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([xml ? xhtml : html], {
      type: xml ? 'application/xhtml+xml' : 'text/html'
    }));
    fetch(frame.src).then(response => response.text()).then(text => {
      fetched.textContent = 'BLOB FETCH OK: ' + text.length + ' characters';
    }).catch(error => { fetched.textContent = String(error); });
  }
  setTimeout(report, 2000);
}
</script>
```

The extended probe also tested sandbox="allow-same-origin allow-scripts", closed shadow roots, visible/initially hidden iframes, and assigning src before insertion. Blob documents remained blank in each case.

Model token limits/context usage: not applicable to this local rendering reproduction.

### What is the expected behavior?

Locally created HTML/XHTML blob URLs should navigate and render in iframes, and complete the relevant load/error lifecycle. If blob iframe navigation is intentionally unsupported, the browser should surface an explicit diagnostic rather than leaving the frame at about:blank while callers wait indefinitely.

### Additional information

Related reports searched before filing:
- https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/37941 — the standalone probe also logged the same MutationObserver.observe non-Node error on an earlier run. The probe itself creates no MutationObserver. This may be related instrumentation behavior; causality is not established.
- https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/21144 — broader in-app Browser iframe inspection/input/screenshot problems. Our failure concerns rendering/navigating a locally created blob iframe, so this is not assumed to be the same issue.

Observed secondary console message:
Uncaught TypeError: Failed to execute 'observe' on 'MutationObserver': parameter 1 is not of type 'Node'.

The reproduction uses generated placeholder strings only.
